LOCALIZATION / SEGMENTATION NOTES
Localization: (x, y, r); r = radius (approx. boundaries irrespective of circularity)
Segmentation: a label per (m x m) pixels (except vessel)

SCALE TABLE: 
- Use percentage-wise radius (1D) & area (2D) per elements present in field of view.

OPTIC DISC
- Use brightness data as the only primary algorithm.
  -> Avoid regions with blood vessel detected (to avoid confusion).
- Use centre-surround: [mean_col(OD) - mean_col(surr)]
  and percentage radius (on FOV) algorithm to confirm.
- Output: (center-x, center-y, radius-r)


VESSELS

(a) Map out vessels of certain pixels (approx. width of main & 1st branch) using MATCHED FILTERING.
  -> pixel true -> 1

(b) Use FRANGI method to pass through all (no min. fixed pixel width) 
  -> venous beading (super high rb) -> 0
  -> major vessel (big rb) -> 1
  -> 1st branch (small rb) -> 2
  -> minor vessel (super small rb) -> 3

(c)
- major vessel - FRANGI - regular -> 0
- neovascularisation (high density) -> 1
- IRMA (low density) -> 2

Concept / labels:
    [x, y] [a] [0, 1, 2, 3] [0, 1, 2]
             (b)          (c)

